a)	Create a new Spring Boot project.
Aim: To bootstrap a structured Spring Boot application via Spring Initializr containing the required dependencies for publishing a SOAP-based web service. 
Procedure:
1.	Navigate to the online initialization interface at [https://start.spring.io/](https://start.spring.io/). 
2.	Configure the project parameters exactly as follows: 
o	Project: Maven Project 
o	Language: Java 
o	Spring Boot: Latest Stable Version 
3.	Click Add Dependencies and select the mandatory module: 
o	Spring Web Services (Provides SOAP web service capabilities, handling XML message parsing and WSDL generation features).
4.	Select Generate to export and download the project bundle zip file. 
5.	Unpack the compressed archive and import the root folder into your IDE (VS Code / IntelliJ). 

