c)	 Implement service using @Service.
Aim: To write the service implementation layer annotated with @Service and populate an internal mock collection to serve incoming SOAP data requests. 
User Domain Model POJO (SoapUser.java):
package com.example.demo.model;

public class SoapUser {
    private Long id;
    private String name;
    private String email;

    public SoapUser() {}

    public SoapUser(Long id, String name, String email) {
        this.id = id;
        this.name = name;
        this.email = email;
    }

    public Long getId() { return id; }
    public void setId(Long id) { this.id = id; }
    public String getName() { return name; }
    public void setName(String name) { this.name = name; }
    public String getEmail() { return email; }
    public void setEmail(String email) { this.email = email; }
}
